1
00:01:37,729 --> 00:01:43,950
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:46,789
[Episode 26]

3
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:54,470
[Chen Junnan]

4
00:01:57,289 --> 00:01:59,020
[Beijing International Hotel]

5
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,920
We're now on Chang'an Avenue,

6
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,280
eating corn.

7
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,760
Two kilometers ahead

8
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,230
is Tian'anmen Square.

9
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,560
Uncle Che,

10
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:09,530
we've arrived at Tian'anmen.

11
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:11,520
[Long Live the People's Republic of China!
Long Live the Great Unity of the Peoples of the World!]

12
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,910
I've brought Uncle Che to see the sea!

13
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:14,960
Look,

14
00:02:15,030 --> 00:02:16,190
Shichahai.

15
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:17,470
I see it, Uncle Che.

16
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:25,560
Two,

17
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,400
one,

18
00:02:26,630 --> 00:02:28,000
cheese!

19
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,130
[Gulou West Street]

20
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:47,720
[Thank you very much
for taking care of my dad.]

21
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:56,360
I'm planning to build the factory

22
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,750
in Yushu County, Fucheng,

23
00:02:57,750 --> 00:02:59,120
because the rent there

24
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:00,680
is at least one-sixth cheaper

25
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,870
than in Shenyang.

26
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:03,710
Plus, the local government

27
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:05,030
offers some policy incentives,

28
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:07,000
which could reduce our costs

29
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,110
by at least 30%.

30
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:09,870
That's great.

31
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,930
I'm not worried about the production

32
00:03:14,150 --> 00:03:15,910
of the neck massager.

33
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:16,710
He asked me to film it.

34
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:17,240
Mainly,

35
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:18,840
r-regarding promotion...

36
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:19,520
Look at him,

37
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:20,680
Commissioner Chen.

38
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,030
How do you plan to handle it?

39
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:23,280
He wants to show you

40
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,280
his hardworking side.

41
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,590
Doing the opposite.

42
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:27,280
He really spruced himself up

43
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,079
this time.

44
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:28,780
Look at him.

45
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:29,960
He's looking

46
00:03:30,470 --> 00:03:31,630
so sharp.

47
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,370
He's even had his hair done.

48
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:36,930
I've never seen him look so polished.

49
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,150
Uncle Che.

50
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:40,350
What are you mumbling about?

51
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:42,480
I'm not allowed to talk?

52
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,150
No.

53
00:03:45,150 --> 00:03:47,680
I want you to take

54
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,470
the minutes.

55
00:03:48,470 --> 00:03:49,800
But you're not only mumbling here.

56
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:52,000
You've got yourself in the footage too.

57
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,460
It could expose us.

58
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:55,970
Understood.

59
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:57,120
I'll make sure the mission is completed.

60
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,840
Thanks for your hard work, Uncle Che.

61
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,030
Call me "comrade."

62
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:02,910
Comrade Che, thanks for your hard work.

63
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,840
Sorry about that, Professor Lin.

64
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:05,800
It's okay.

65
00:04:06,150 --> 00:04:07,630
What's he mumbling about?

66
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:28,410
[Congrats on finding a new direction.
Keep going!]

67
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:31,630
[Congrats on finding a new direction.
Keep going!]

68
00:04:32,890 --> 00:04:33,140
[Che Mingming]

69
00:04:35,510 --> 00:04:36,159
Uncle Che.

70
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,680
Is the big city fun?

71
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,560
It is quite fun.

72
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,560
It's just that...

73
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:44,310
Isn't your job a bit too tiring?

74
00:04:44,310 --> 00:04:46,040
You've never worked in a big city.

75
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:53,850
[Traditional Beijing Fried Sauce Noodles]

76
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,770
How would you know if it's hard?

77
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,750
You're just lucky

78
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,800
you have a generous boss now.

79
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:54,800
Think about your...

80
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,920
your last job.

81
00:04:56,510 --> 00:04:57,480
Every now and then,

82
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,390
you'd sneak off to some little corner,

83
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:00,390
find some old piece of cardboard,

84
00:05:00,390 --> 00:05:01,950
lie down on it,
and secretly scroll through your phone.

85
00:05:01,950 --> 00:05:03,360
Didn't that make you feel pretty happy?

86
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:04,750
That's nothing compared to now, right?

87
00:05:04,750 --> 00:05:05,430
Am I right?

88
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,480
How did you know?

89
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:09,070
Have you got cameras on me or something?

90
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:11,040
You're something else, Uncle Che.

91
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:11,720
Eat more.

92
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:13,240
Should I order another plate for you?

93
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,190
It's not easy

94
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,430
making money in a big city,
and the cost of living is high.

95
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:17,750
You should watch your spending.

96
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:19,270
My salary is pretty good now.

97
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:20,920
Besides, treating you to a meal

98
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:21,720
is no big deal.

99
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:23,750
Save when you can; spend when you must.

100
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:24,360
If you've got

101
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,680
some money to spare,

102
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,040
you can help out your brother a little.

103
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,600
Why would he need my help?

104
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:31,360
He's been back at work
for less than a month

105
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,870
and hasn't gotten his salary yet.

106
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:35,330
And he spent a lot
on Jia Xin's medical bills.

107
00:05:35,950 --> 00:05:37,350
Jia Xin's medical bills?

108
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:38,950
What happened to him?

109
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,510
You don't know?

110
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:43,190
No, I don't.

111
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:50,400
[Your Strength Is Our Guiding Light]

112
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,380
How are you feeling today?

113
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,480
Much better.

114
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:53,390
Does it still hurt
when they change your dressing?

115
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:54,190
It does,

116
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,659
but it's much better than before.

117
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:58,330
I can just tough it out now.

118
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,190
Keep the wound clean

119
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:02,120
and dry.

120
00:06:02,830 --> 00:06:03,830
More importantly,

121
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:05,160
keep a good mindset.

122
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,210
Zhengliang,

123
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:08,490
[Xiaoximen Hospital
Affiliated with Qikang Medical]

124
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:07,510
don't worry.

125
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,190
That kind of thing

126
00:06:08,490 --> 00:06:09,210
[Burn Ward]

127
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,240
won't happen again.

128
00:06:09,270 --> 00:06:10,410
[Keep quiet]

129
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,430
I've come to realize something.

130
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:14,040
You only live once.

131
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,190
I can't just give up,

132
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:15,920
right?

133
00:06:20,190 --> 00:06:21,120
What's going on?

134
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,290
Why are you back?

135
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:29,920
How...

136
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:31,750
How did you end up

137
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:32,950
looking like this?

138
00:06:34,270 --> 00:06:37,830
You never know what life has in store.

139
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,390
I went to take on

140
00:06:39,390 --> 00:06:40,480
the King of Hell.

141
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,680
I won.

142
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:42,950
Zhengliang saved me.

143
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:45,060
Zhengguang, you're here.

144
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,430
You guys talk.

145
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:15,920
I'm full.

146
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:17,560
Okay.

147
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:22,170
How did you find out?

148
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:23,920
Junnan told me.

149
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,160
Why didn't you tell me?

150
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,360
What for?

151
00:07:29,270 --> 00:07:31,730
I didn't want you
worrying too much about me.

152
00:07:33,159 --> 00:07:34,480
That's not being a real friend.

153
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,159
I'm not being a real friend?

154
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,800
L-Look at the state I'm in.

155
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:40,040
I-I was afraid I'd hold you back

156
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,840
and stop you from getting ahead.

157
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:43,070
I wouldn't

158
00:07:43,070 --> 00:07:45,000
just stand by and watch you fall.

159
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:50,360
Well, I got back up, didn't I?

160
00:07:51,190 --> 00:07:54,050
And I... haven't exactly
made something of myself.

161
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:55,450
It doesn't matter.

162
00:07:56,430 --> 00:07:57,950
Zhengguang, have a seat.

163
00:07:58,190 --> 00:07:59,520
Sit down and let's talk.

164
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,240
I am... sitting.

165
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:04,330
I've b-been sitting this whole time.

166
00:08:13,870 --> 00:08:14,630
Zhengguang.

167
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,020
We want to get married next month.

168
00:08:28,870 --> 00:08:29,480
Well...

169
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,720
You two haven't known each other long,

170
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,430
and you're already talking about marriage?

171
00:08:31,430 --> 00:08:32,559
Isn't that too fast?

172
00:08:33,030 --> 00:08:33,669
I...

173
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,120
Some connections aren't measured by time.

174
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:38,190
It was love at first sight for us.

175
00:08:46,030 --> 00:08:47,290
L-Love at first sight?

176
00:08:49,390 --> 00:08:50,850
Love at first sight, okay.

177
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,150
Are...

178
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,080
Are you against us getting married?

179
00:08:58,550 --> 00:08:59,670
What are you talking about?

180
00:08:59,670 --> 00:09:00,870
Why would I be against it?

181
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:02,330
What is there to object to?

182
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,720
And who am I to object?

183
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:04,550
I support it.

184
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:05,810
I strongly support it.

185
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,960
It's a good thing.

186
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,360
Something to celebrate.

187
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:10,860
Zhengguang...

188
00:09:12,750 --> 00:09:14,720
I didn't know how to tell you.

189
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,440
I just...

190
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,570
You could've sent me

191
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,620
a WeChat message or called me.

192
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:20,840
And if all else failed, you could've

193
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,480
written me a letter
or sent a carrier pigeon.

194
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,960
What's so hard about telling me?

195
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:25,820
You really know how to make a fuss.

196
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:26,720
Listen,

197
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,790
when I was in Beijing

198
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:28,840
and heard what happened to you,

199
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,030
I was so upset.

200
00:09:30,390 --> 00:09:31,910
It felt like the worst news imaginable.

201
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:33,170
But then I came back...

202
00:09:33,910 --> 00:09:36,110
and now I've heard some wonderful news.

203
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:39,120
My heartfelt congratulations to you both.

204
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,720
I'm genuinely happy for you.

205
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:41,390
Really.

206
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,260
Congratulations in advance.

207
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:47,760
Be sure to invite me
to the wedding banquet.

208
00:09:49,330 --> 00:09:52,420
[Your Health, Our Expertise]

209
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:55,730
[Xiaoximen Hospital
Affiliated with Qikang Medical]

210
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,110
Let's chat.

211
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,900
Can't you see I'm working?

212
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,550
I know.

213
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,120
I registered as a patient.

214
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:16,720
Besides, you don't have
any patients waiting.

215
00:10:19,630 --> 00:10:20,440
You usually can't even be bothered

216
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,600
to say a few words to me.

217
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,240
You were only in Beijing for a few days,

218
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,440
and you miss me that much already?

219
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,670
Don't flatter yourself.

220
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:27,120
I just couldn't find
anyone else to talk to.

221
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,320
If there'd been
even one other person available,

222
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:30,520
I definitely wouldn't have come to you.

223
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,920
Alright, tell me. What's up?

224
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,510
Jia Xin and Gong Xue are getting married.

225
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:41,840
Isn't that a good thing?

226
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,910
We'll have to give them gift money, right?

227
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:46,000
I'm broke.

228
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,330
Can you lend me 800 yuan?

229
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:48,840
No!

230
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:49,720
Fine, don't lend it to me then.

231
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,920
Why are you shouting?

232
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:58,550
Dr. Yang!

233
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:01,080
Keep an eye on things for me for a bit.

234
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:05,910
Come on, come out with me.

235
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:12,200
You like Gong Xue?

236
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:20,670
[Accessible Route]

237
00:11:15,870 --> 00:11:17,600
Why did you come back this time?

238
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,750
Junnan told me
Jia Xin tried to end his life,

239
00:11:19,750 --> 00:11:21,350
so I came back to support him.

240
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:22,480
He's over it now.

241
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:23,360
You can go back.

242
00:11:25,150 --> 00:11:25,960
If I just leave like this,

243
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:26,630
wouldn't it look like

244
00:11:26,630 --> 00:11:27,550
I can't get over it?

245
00:11:27,550 --> 00:11:29,000
What's there to get over?

246
00:11:29,150 --> 00:11:30,480
Why are you so entitled?

247
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:32,870
Just because you like Gong Xue,

248
00:11:32,870 --> 00:11:34,480
does she have to like you back?

249
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:35,810
I don't think like that.

250
00:11:36,270 --> 00:11:37,550
When I decided to go to Beijing,

251
00:11:37,550 --> 00:11:38,750
I'd already let it go.

252
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,460
But now that they're getting married...

253
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:43,670
it still hurts.

254
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:45,200
What's there to hurt about?

255
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,750
I think you just have too much free time.

256
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:47,550
Get back to Beijing.

257
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:48,550
You'll feel better once you get busy.

258
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:50,010
You were the one who told me

259
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:52,220
to come back whenever I got tired.

260
00:11:53,870 --> 00:11:54,840
I did say that.

261
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,550
But later Chen Junnan told me

262
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,610
you were doing quite well in Beijing.

263
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,910
Now that you've got a good opportunity,

264
00:11:59,910 --> 00:12:01,240
shouldn't you seize it?

265
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:04,440
No.

266
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,320
Jia Xin is my buddy.

267
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,150
I got him the job

268
00:12:07,150 --> 00:12:08,080
at the crematorium.

269
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:10,030
Now that things have turned out like this,

270
00:12:10,030 --> 00:12:12,160
I have to take responsibility for him.

271
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:16,790
Zhengguang.

272
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,870
He doesn't need you
to take responsibility for him.

273
00:12:20,870 --> 00:12:22,670
Showing that you care is enough.

274
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,440
You really don't understand anything.

275
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,240
I'm not going to waste my breath.

276
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:31,670
You're leaving just like that?

277
00:12:31,670 --> 00:12:37,420
[Accessible Route]

278
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:32,720
How about I prescribe you

279
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,050
some antidepressants?

280
00:12:34,910 --> 00:12:36,240
Save them for yourself.

281
00:12:37,850 --> 00:12:43,740
[Accessible Route]

282
00:12:50,150 --> 00:12:51,080
Uncle Che?

283
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:08,510
Mr. Wang.

284
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:10,080
Did you see

285
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,080
the old man who came with me earlier?

286
00:13:12,870 --> 00:13:14,270
He went to his workplace.

287
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,370
No, wait.

288
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:17,730
Are we talking about the same person?

289
00:13:17,870 --> 00:13:19,000
Don't you know

290
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,030
the old man's status?

291
00:13:20,030 --> 00:13:20,720
No, no.

292
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:23,010
I was flustered and forgot.

293
00:13:23,030 --> 00:13:23,840
Forgot?

294
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,000
Just because your boss

295
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
is down-to-earth doesn't mean

296
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,840
you should forget he's still your boss.

297
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:28,510
Yes, yes.

298
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,360
Well,

299
00:13:29,790 --> 00:13:30,720
did he give you

300
00:13:30,790 --> 00:13:32,030
the address of his workplace?

301
00:13:32,030 --> 00:13:33,440
I-I have to go pick him up.

302
00:13:33,810 --> 00:13:36,890
[Restricted Research Area; Authorized Personnel Only;
No Photography; No Video Recording]

303
00:13:42,610 --> 00:13:52,350
[Beijing Taxi]

304
00:13:45,030 --> 00:13:46,150
Here, sir.

305
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,030
Thank you.

306
00:13:53,110 --> 00:14:01,330
[No Parking;
Violators Will Be Heavily Penalized]

307
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:12,160
Uncle Che, why did you come here?

308
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,780
This is where you used to work?

309
00:14:25,750 --> 00:14:26,720
Stay here and don't wander off.

310
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:27,390
Wait for me.

311
00:14:35,030 --> 00:14:35,390
Hello.

312
00:14:35,390 --> 00:14:36,200
Hello, sir.

313
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,080
Um...

314
00:14:38,510 --> 00:14:40,370
That old man across the street...

315
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Did he do anything

316
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:43,910
strange?

317
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:44,840
No.

318
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,570
He's just been standing there.

319
00:14:49,910 --> 00:14:50,790
He's my dad.

320
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:53,390
He has Alzheimer's.

321
00:14:53,750 --> 00:14:55,080
His memory

322
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:57,000
comes and goes.

323
00:14:57,270 --> 00:14:57,840
Can you

324
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,000
do me a favor in a bit?

325
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,330
I'll bring him over,

326
00:15:00,390 --> 00:15:01,250
and I'll ask you

327
00:15:01,390 --> 00:15:03,510
if you know Comrade Che Changhai.

328
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,360
Just say you do.

329
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:07,860
[Public Welfare]

330
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:06,360
Is that okay?

331
00:15:14,550 --> 00:15:15,360
Uncle Che.

332
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:16,670
I asked the young guard

333
00:15:16,670 --> 00:15:17,480
over there.

334
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:18,360
He said

335
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,750
you used to work there.

336
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,090
Let's go over and chat with him.

337
00:15:27,150 --> 00:15:28,080
Let's go back.

338
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:30,840
Go back where?

339
00:15:41,270 --> 00:15:42,910
Back to the hotel.

340
00:15:44,550 --> 00:15:45,440
To the station.

341
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,170
Back to Fucheng.

342
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:52,510
We're already here.

343
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,550
Let's go visit your old workplace.

344
00:15:54,550 --> 00:15:55,360
Let's go.

345
00:15:56,510 --> 00:15:57,440
There's no need.

346
00:16:08,030 --> 00:16:09,270
I'm retired.

347
00:16:09,970 --> 00:16:13,970
[Science City]

348
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:20,360
Congratulations to Comrade Che Changhai

349
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,260
on his honorable retirement!

350
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:37,320
Junnan.

351
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,000
Mingming.

352
00:16:38,390 --> 00:16:39,550
I just wanted to let you know

353
00:16:39,550 --> 00:16:40,720
that your dad and I are at the station.

354
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,440
We'll board in an hour.

355
00:16:42,870 --> 00:16:43,720
So, don't worry.

356
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:44,850
Everything's fine.

357
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:45,870
Thank you

358
00:16:45,870 --> 00:16:46,870
for taking care of my dad
these past few days.

359
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:48,070
It must've been hard.

360
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,720
I'll treat you to a meal
when you get back.

361
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:50,720
It was no trouble.

362
00:16:53,030 --> 00:16:53,840
There's something

363
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:55,370
I don't know how to tell you.

364
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:57,190
What's wrong with my dad?

365
00:16:58,390 --> 00:16:58,870
Nothing.

366
00:16:58,870 --> 00:17:00,360
He's fine. Everything is normal.

367
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,600
Is he acting up again?

368
00:17:02,030 --> 00:17:03,630
What ridiculous thing did he do this time?

369
00:17:03,630 --> 00:17:04,349
If he caused trouble

370
00:17:04,349 --> 00:17:04,829
and we need to pay compensation,

371
00:17:04,829 --> 00:17:05,750
you have to tell me.

372
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:06,829
I-I'll give you the money.

373
00:17:06,829 --> 00:17:07,680
No.

374
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,160
Relax.

375
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:09,960
It's just...

376
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,240
He's been unusually quiet
these past few days.

377
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:19,839
His behavior and speech
have been a bit off.

378
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:22,530
Do you understand what I'm getting at?

379
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:23,240
I don't.

380
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,270
I...

381
00:17:26,069 --> 00:17:27,880
A-Anyway, as long as he's fine.

382
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:31,680
Uncle Che.

383
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:35,810
Why aren't you reading the newspaper?

384
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:38,270
Eight pages.

385
00:17:38,590 --> 00:17:40,190
I've read all the headlines.

386
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:41,510
There's nothing

387
00:17:41,510 --> 00:17:43,040
worth paying attention to.

388
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:45,880
I'm done reading.

389
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:50,440
Stop crying.

390
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,770
We'll have your dad fix it
when we get home.

391
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,000
Stop crying!

392
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,960
You dropped it yourself.
Who can you blame?

393
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:59,680
Hold it in! You child...

394
00:18:00,510 --> 00:18:01,550
Do you hear me?

395
00:18:03,590 --> 00:18:04,200
I got it.

396
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,860
What are you doing, Uncle Che?

397
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,480
Do you hear me? Stop crying!

398
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:10,270
Hold it in!

399
00:18:11,110 --> 00:18:12,040
Hey, little one.

400
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:15,570
Let Grandpa show you a magic trick.

401
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:17,160
A magic trick.

402
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:28,310
Is that a good one?

403
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:29,880
Here, take it.

404
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:30,310
This... This...

405
00:18:30,310 --> 00:18:31,550
We can't take this. Thank you.

406
00:18:31,550 --> 00:18:32,200
We can't spoil the kid.

407
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:32,880
Oh, come on.

408
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:33,790
It's fate that we ended up

409
00:18:33,790 --> 00:18:34,990
in the same train car.

410
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:35,480
It's just a handicraft.

411
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,400
Not worth much.

412
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:37,350
Here, take it.

413
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:40,030
Is it fun?

414
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:41,680
It's fun.

415
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:42,680
Take it.

416
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:43,940
Quick, thank Grandpa.

417
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,070
Thank you, Grandpa.

418
00:18:45,070 --> 00:18:46,270
You're welcome.

419
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:47,810
How old are you, kid?

420
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:48,590
Eight.

421
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:49,480
Impressive.

422
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:51,000
What's your name?

423
00:18:51,350 --> 00:18:52,160
Xiaobo.

424
00:18:54,270 --> 00:18:55,270
What's your name?

425
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,400
My name's Xiaobo.

426
00:19:00,830 --> 00:19:01,830
Well then...

427
00:19:02,310 --> 00:19:04,310
Study hard and keep striving to improve.

428
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:05,240
Okay, that's it.

429
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:06,000
Thank you.

430
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:13,550
Uncle Che,

431
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,530
why did you give away

432
00:19:16,350 --> 00:19:17,750
the organization's key?

433
00:19:18,830 --> 00:19:19,640
What organization?

434
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:20,440
What key?

435
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:25,720
Never mind.

436
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,780
Just pretend I was talking nonsense.

437
00:19:29,590 --> 00:19:30,720
Commissioner Chen.

438
00:19:32,030 --> 00:19:32,920
Well, I was so busy looking at

439
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,310
the scenery that I forgot to ask:

440
00:19:34,310 --> 00:19:36,910
didn't you go to Beijing
to discuss the patent?

441
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:38,350
How did it go?

442
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:39,700
It went quite well.

443
00:19:39,830 --> 00:19:42,490
Both sides are interested in
working together.

444
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:43,790
Good, good.

445
00:19:45,070 --> 00:19:45,830
Well...

446
00:19:48,070 --> 00:19:49,030
I actually know

447
00:19:49,030 --> 00:19:50,630
a thing or two about patents.

448
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:52,200
You see, from filing the application

449
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:54,880
to getting it approved,

450
00:19:55,030 --> 00:19:56,480
then moving into mass production,

451
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,030
and finally bringing
the product to market—

452
00:19:58,030 --> 00:20:00,360
it's a very long and complicated process.

453
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,940
It's better to be careful.

454
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:04,070
You need to do thorough research

455
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:05,130
and stay cautious.

456
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,840
That way, you won't go wrong.

457
00:20:08,830 --> 00:20:10,030
You're right.

458
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,790
You must be exhausted. Get some good rest.

459
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:21,480
I'm fine.

460
00:20:23,750 --> 00:20:24,550
Come on.

461
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:26,880
It's still warmer inside.

462
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:27,720
Uncle Che, Mingming,

463
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:29,160
you two get some rest.

464
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,000
I won't come in.

465
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:30,440
I still have something to do.

466
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:31,070
Thank you.

467
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:32,270
No, no, don't go!

468
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:32,960
Come in and sit for a while.

469
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:34,480
I've got things to do. Really.

470
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:35,680
You have things to do?

471
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:36,480
Alright then.

472
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:37,440
Junnan.

473
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:38,350
Thank you for taking care of me

474
00:20:38,350 --> 00:20:39,350
in Beijing.

475
00:20:39,350 --> 00:20:39,950
Thank you.

476
00:20:40,790 --> 00:20:42,120
Thanks for what you did.

477
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:44,160
Well, Junnan,

478
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:46,790
I think you're so much better

479
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:47,960
than Zhang Hao.

480
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:51,250
Give our Mingming a chance.

481
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:51,830
Mingming is...

482
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:53,400
Dad, what are you talking about?

483
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,640
What?

484
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:55,960
I can't

485
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,420
stay by your side forever.

486
00:20:57,550 --> 00:20:59,240
In the end, the world is a lonely place

487
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,720
when you have no one,

488
00:21:01,070 --> 00:21:01,640
right?

489
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:05,240
As for our plan of action from here,

490
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,240
I'll leave you two to discuss it.

491
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:07,880
Okay.

492
00:21:08,310 --> 00:21:09,640
I'll go over it with her.

493
00:21:17,830 --> 00:21:19,030
So this is what you meant when you said

494
00:21:19,030 --> 00:21:20,160
his behavior was strangely normal?

495
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:20,960
Can you tell

496
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:22,960
which of your dad's remarks are made
when he's lucid?

497
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:23,790
I can.

498
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:27,960
Uncle Che, what's wrong?

499
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:28,680
Nothing.

500
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:29,830
N-Nothing.

501
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:31,310
You two continue.

502
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:36,880
What exactly

503
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:38,410
did you tell my dad about us?

504
00:21:38,830 --> 00:21:40,240
What's there between us?

505
00:21:45,350 --> 00:21:47,000
I really don't have the energy
to think about...

506
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:47,880
Okay, okay.

507
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:49,480
I know.

508
00:21:49,750 --> 00:21:50,550
Don't worry.

509
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,440
I won't put you on the spot.

510
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:04,440
Whenever I come back to Fucheng,

511
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:05,350
I always make a point of coming here

512
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:06,750
to spend some time alone.

513
00:22:08,550 --> 00:22:10,010
Shenzhen also has the sea,

514
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:13,210
but I still prefer the sea here
in Fucheng.

515
00:22:13,310 --> 00:22:14,110
Why?

516
00:22:15,830 --> 00:22:17,290
I can't really explain it.

517
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:19,750
Maybe all seas are the same,

518
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:21,440
but I always feel

519
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,310
there's a sweetness in the air

520
00:22:22,310 --> 00:22:23,270
here in Fucheng.

521
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:26,790
And

522
00:22:26,830 --> 00:22:29,160
the colder it gets, the sweeter it smells.

523
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,480
Actually, I've been dreaming about
my mom a lot lately.

524
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:35,270
Really?

525
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:37,030
Ever since I came back,

526
00:22:37,030 --> 00:22:39,240
I've been dreaming about her all the time.

527
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:40,970
Sometimes, it doesn't even...

528
00:22:41,790 --> 00:22:42,790
feel like a dream.

529
00:22:43,110 --> 00:22:44,160
It feels so real.

530
00:22:45,750 --> 00:22:47,400
As if she were sitting right beside me,

531
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,310
talking to me.

532
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:52,960
I even dreamed about her a few days ago.

533
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:53,750
Really?

534
00:22:55,070 --> 00:22:55,750
But it seems like

535
00:22:55,750 --> 00:22:56,590
I've been dreaming about her

536
00:22:56,590 --> 00:22:57,790
less and less lately.

537
00:23:00,550 --> 00:23:01,720
Maybe that's thanks to me,

538
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:02,550
huh?

539
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,030
Because she's not
so worried about you anymore,

540
00:23:06,030 --> 00:23:07,960
and she doesn't miss you quite as much.

541
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:08,750
Right?

542
00:23:09,750 --> 00:23:10,680
Making the trip

543
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:11,960
back and forth must be

544
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,090
exhausting for her.

545
00:23:17,510 --> 00:23:18,240
Once you get

546
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,880
your reading disorder sorted out,

547
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,440
what's the first thing you want to do?

548
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:24,440
Definitely keep working toward
my driver's license.

549
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,070
Although it's been pretty tough—

550
00:23:26,070 --> 00:23:27,670
learning while throwing up—

551
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:29,610
I'm finally making some progress.

552
00:23:30,110 --> 00:23:32,270
At least I passed the driving theory test.

553
00:23:32,270 --> 00:23:33,130
I'll keep at it.

554
00:23:34,590 --> 00:23:35,450
What about you?

555
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:37,830
If your phobia could be completely cured,

556
00:23:37,830 --> 00:23:39,310
what would you want to do most?

557
00:23:39,310 --> 00:23:40,110
Me?

558
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:44,680
What I want most is to see snow fall here.

559
00:23:45,510 --> 00:23:46,880
You want to see snow?

560
00:23:48,270 --> 00:23:49,480
My phone says

561
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,110
it'll snow early this month.

562
00:23:51,790 --> 00:23:53,120
Let me take you to see it.

563
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:55,720
Aren't you afraid I'll pass out?

564
00:23:55,830 --> 00:23:57,350
Wouldn't that be perfect?

565
00:23:59,750 --> 00:24:00,680
What do you mean?

566
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,080
I'd go get us a hotel room.

567
00:24:02,720 --> 00:24:04,160
A snow-view room.

568
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,510
Indeed.

569
00:24:12,510 --> 00:24:13,680
You're indeed much more interesting

570
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:15,010
than my ex-girlfriend.

571
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,740
What's wrong with you?

572
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:21,830
I should just

573
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:23,240
slap you into the sea!

574
00:24:24,310 --> 00:24:26,110
Do you even know how to talk to people?

575
00:24:26,110 --> 00:24:26,830
Well, obviously!

576
00:24:26,830 --> 00:24:29,090
Of course I'm more interesting than her!

577
00:24:33,590 --> 00:24:35,520
I think you're quite interesting.

578
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,110
The paperwork's all done.

579
00:25:21,110 --> 00:25:21,910
Let's go home.

580
00:25:24,350 --> 00:25:25,810
I'm going to the restroom.

581
00:25:26,270 --> 00:25:27,160
Want me to come with you?

582
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:27,590
It's fine.

583
00:25:27,590 --> 00:25:28,790
I can manage on my own.

584
00:25:38,270 --> 00:25:39,270
I'll go too.

585
00:25:39,270 --> 00:25:41,200
I'll leave the papers here for you.

586
00:25:57,830 --> 00:25:58,640
Jia,

587
00:25:59,070 --> 00:26:00,330
which stall are you in?

588
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:06,240
Here.

589
00:26:06,830 --> 00:26:07,830
I'll be right out.

590
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:09,030
No rush.

591
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:14,570
Are you scared of me?

592
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:16,130
What? Am I crazy?

593
00:26:16,590 --> 00:26:17,480
You're my buddy.

594
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:19,010
Why would I be scared of you?

595
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:22,160
Do I look scarier

596
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:23,270
than a ghost now?

597
00:26:25,590 --> 00:26:28,320
Then you're giving ghosts
way too little credit.

598
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:37,560
You say that
like you've actually seen one.

599
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:41,510
It's fine.

600
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:42,880
My brother said

601
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:44,210
you can get a skin graft.

602
00:26:46,590 --> 00:26:47,720
It's too expensive.

603
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:50,500
And I'd need several operations.

604
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:53,400
Let's leave it at that.

605
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,530
I'm not getting one.

606
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:58,550
You can't decide not to
get one just like that.

607
00:26:58,550 --> 00:27:00,030
Wait until we get rich.

608
00:27:00,030 --> 00:27:01,090
When we have money,

609
00:27:01,310 --> 00:27:02,160
you can get

610
00:27:02,440 --> 00:27:03,900
as many grafts as you want.

611
00:27:03,920 --> 00:27:04,720
Right?

612
00:27:10,550 --> 00:27:12,750
I'll never make it big in this lifetime.

613
00:27:14,160 --> 00:27:16,030
Looking... Looking like this,

614
00:27:16,030 --> 00:27:17,560
I won't get hired anywhere.

615
00:27:20,550 --> 00:27:21,810
Maybe in the next life.

616
00:27:26,790 --> 00:27:27,590
Jia Xin.

617
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:30,160
I'm officially extending

618
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:31,750
an invitation to you today.

619
00:27:32,350 --> 00:27:34,010
I'm going to start a business.

620
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,550
I really need you.

621
00:27:35,590 --> 00:27:37,190
And I can't do it without you.

622
00:27:37,720 --> 00:27:38,550
I'm telling you,
if you don't come on board,

623
00:27:38,550 --> 00:27:40,000
the whole business is going to fall apart.

624
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:41,530
Can you help your buddy out?

625
00:28:03,310 --> 00:28:04,770
You're back, Zhengliang.

626
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:06,720
Come here.

627
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:09,540
I need to discuss something with you.

628
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:12,110
What's wrong?

629
00:28:15,070 --> 00:28:15,880
Go ahead.

630
00:28:16,030 --> 00:28:16,890
I'm listening.

631
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:22,520
I want to sell the apartment.

632
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,000
Okay.

633
00:28:26,030 --> 00:28:27,290
You agreed so readily.

634
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:30,320
So you have no feelings
for this place, huh?

635
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:32,680
Zhengguang, you know me.

636
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:34,350
I've been bad at

637
00:28:35,110 --> 00:28:37,370
expressing myself ever since I was a kid.

638
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:38,640
But I'm human too.

639
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:40,460
Of course I have feelings.

640
00:28:41,440 --> 00:28:42,350
My feelings

641
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:43,920
are for Mom

642
00:28:44,750 --> 00:28:45,510
and you,

643
00:28:46,440 --> 00:28:48,100
not for some physical object.

644
00:28:50,070 --> 00:28:50,880
Besides, last time you said

645
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:52,350
you wanted to go to Beijing,

646
00:28:52,350 --> 00:28:54,680
didn't I agree to
sell this place then too?

647
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:57,110
Now that you've

648
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:58,270
brought it up again,

649
00:28:58,830 --> 00:29:00,690
you must really be short on money.

650
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:02,880
So let's sell it.

651
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:06,680
I can rent a place

652
00:29:07,310 --> 00:29:08,370
near the hospital.

653
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:10,790
Rent in Fucheng is cheap anyway.

654
00:29:13,270 --> 00:29:14,070
It's fine.

655
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:17,420
Rent is cheap, but so are housing prices.

656
00:29:18,110 --> 00:29:19,910
It probably won't sell for much.

657
00:29:20,350 --> 00:29:21,750
I don't know if it'll be enough.

658
00:29:21,750 --> 00:29:22,680
What do you mean?

659
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:24,350
What are you planning?

660
00:29:24,350 --> 00:29:25,950
Why do you need so much money?

661
00:29:27,590 --> 00:29:29,750
I'm... not going back to Beijing.

662
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:31,590
I'm staying in Fucheng

663
00:29:31,590 --> 00:29:33,240
and starting a small business.

664
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:34,880
You have to think this through.

665
00:29:34,880 --> 00:29:35,680
Some opportunities, once missed,

666
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:36,480
are gone.

667
00:29:36,550 --> 00:29:38,210
Don't regret it in a few years.

668
00:29:39,160 --> 00:29:40,560
I've thought it through.

669
00:29:41,160 --> 00:29:41,920
Although I

670
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:44,130
didn't spend very long in Beijing,

671
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:46,350
I suddenly understood what it's like

672
00:29:46,350 --> 00:29:47,240
to be alone in an unfamiliar city,

673
00:29:47,240 --> 00:29:49,240
with no friends or family to turn to.

674
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:50,920
I finally understand

675
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:51,510
how hard it's been for you

676
00:29:51,510 --> 00:29:53,160
all these years, living alone

677
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:53,960
in the South.

678
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:55,000
Hold on.

679
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,490
I don't have any friends

680
00:29:57,550 --> 00:29:59,610
because I don't want to make friends.

681
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:02,560
What are you laughing at?

682
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:03,830
As you work hard

683
00:30:03,830 --> 00:30:04,680
to build a better future,

684
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:05,480
you'll definitely meet

685
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:07,340
new friends who share your goals.

686
00:30:08,240 --> 00:30:09,200
Besides,

687
00:30:09,350 --> 00:30:10,640
you haven't known Jia Xin

688
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:11,550
for that long.

689
00:30:14,350 --> 00:30:15,480
I've made up my mind.

690
00:30:15,590 --> 00:30:16,480
I have to stay

691
00:30:17,030 --> 00:30:17,960
and help Jia Xin.

692
00:30:20,960 --> 00:30:22,560
How are you going to help him?

693
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:26,110
What kind of business could you start
that would help him?

694
00:30:26,110 --> 00:30:27,840
I haven't figured that out yet.

695
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:29,850
Liu Zhengguang.

696
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:32,790
You didn't

697
00:30:32,790 --> 00:30:34,790
decide this unilaterally, did you?

698
00:30:35,590 --> 00:30:36,400
You're worried he won't

699
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:37,930
be able to find a decent job?

700
00:30:45,110 --> 00:30:46,680
Stop flattering yourself.

701
00:30:46,920 --> 00:30:48,240
Does he even need your help?

702
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:49,270
I got Jia Xin

703
00:30:49,270 --> 00:30:50,800
the job at the crematorium.

704
00:30:55,030 --> 00:30:56,030
Say you come across someone on the road

705
00:30:56,030 --> 00:30:56,960
who's sick,

706
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:58,200
and you take him to the hospital,

707
00:30:58,200 --> 00:30:59,920
but the doctors fail to save him.

708
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:00,960
Does that make it your fault?

709
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:01,400
That's

710
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,510
not the same thing.

711
00:31:02,510 --> 00:31:03,680
How is it not the same thing?

712
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:05,210
Being responsible is good,

713
00:31:05,270 --> 00:31:05,880
but you can't take responsibility

714
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:07,540
for everything that happens.

715
00:31:07,750 --> 00:31:08,510
What about you, then?

716
00:31:08,510 --> 00:31:09,030
What about me?

717
00:31:09,030 --> 00:31:10,270
Dad took you out to play,

718
00:31:10,270 --> 00:31:11,640
showed off, and died.

719
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:13,200
What did that have to do with you?

720
00:31:13,200 --> 00:31:14,000
Why have you been unable to

721
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,400
let it go all these years?

722
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:24,960
I'm sorry.

723
00:31:26,310 --> 00:31:28,570
I shouldn't have used that as an example.

724
00:31:39,030 --> 00:31:39,830
It's okay.

725
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:42,830
You're right.

726
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:46,460
Dad's death had nothing to do with me.

727
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:49,110
And Jia Xin's burns

728
00:31:49,110 --> 00:31:51,040
have nothing to do with you either.

729
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:52,160
I know.

730
00:31:53,310 --> 00:31:54,160
I know too.

731
00:32:02,790 --> 00:32:03,880
Good grief.

732
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:07,480
That DNA test was a waste of time.

733
00:32:08,790 --> 00:32:10,850
We're brothers through and through.

734
00:32:12,340 --> 00:32:15,490
♪ A soul that came to earth
amid the cries ♪

735
00:32:15,940 --> 00:32:19,110
♪ Welcome to this city of haste ♪

736
00:32:19,550 --> 00:32:21,910
♪ Grow taller, quick as you can ♪

737
00:32:22,210 --> 00:32:24,470
♪ Learn how to find your footing ♪

738
00:32:23,240 --> 00:32:24,570
This bedroom's decent.

739
00:32:25,270 --> 00:32:26,350
Let's have a look at the living room.

740
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:27,000
Okay.

741
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:30,110
♪ A soul who hid
among the lanes and alleys ♪

742
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:28,600
Go check the balcony.

743
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:30,830
Including the TV,

744
00:32:30,510 --> 00:32:33,780
♪ A single turn, and the lamp
at the door grows distant ♪

745
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:33,060
everything was bought new this year.

746
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:36,110
And the entire place has a river view.

747
00:32:34,110 --> 00:32:36,500
♪ The ticket bears no way back ♪

748
00:32:36,270 --> 00:32:37,550
The natural light is excellent too.

749
00:32:36,790 --> 00:32:39,180
♪ How like life it is ♪

750
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:40,040
Isn't that the crematorium across the way?

751
00:32:41,280 --> 00:32:44,630
♪ You'll pass through the seasons,
through dawn and dusk ♪

752
00:32:44,970 --> 00:32:48,170
♪ Hearing someone call your name,
again and again ♪

753
00:32:48,490 --> 00:32:50,940
♪ These ties may hurt a little ♪

754
00:32:51,380 --> 00:32:53,590
♪ Don't heal a broken heart ♪

755
00:32:55,860 --> 00:32:59,130
♪ It will bear witness
to the life you bravely lived ♪

756
00:32:59,380 --> 00:33:02,750
♪ To the beautiful souls you've loved ♪

757
00:33:03,040 --> 00:33:05,550
♪ To the address you call home ♪

758
00:33:04,060 --> 00:33:05,190
[Submit]

759
00:33:05,290 --> 00:33:05,900
[Payment Status: Paid]

760
00:33:05,760 --> 00:33:08,520
♪ In the little town
you've wandered through ♪

761
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:07,210
[Review Status: Submitted;
Pending Review by the Institution Applied To]

762
00:33:07,230 --> 00:33:09,060
[Chaoyang Medical University;
PhD Application System]

763
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:13,730
♪ The wind in the city ♪

764
00:33:14,050 --> 00:33:16,790
♪ Blows through dreams
that flicker between light and dark ♪

765
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:20,540
♪ Blows through one soul's radiance ♪

766
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:24,510
♪ And all its weathered scars ♪

767
00:33:25,890 --> 00:33:28,160
♪ Blows through the depths of winter ♪

768
00:33:28,450 --> 00:33:31,400
♪ Stumbling along in the wind ♪

769
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:34,930
♪ Flickering along in the wind ♪

770
00:33:36,540 --> 00:33:42,470
♪ Toward the crossroads
brimming with sunlight ♪

771
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:42,720
Here, the keys.

772
00:33:45,830 --> 00:33:49,280
♪ May every road you take be safe ♪

773
00:33:49,580 --> 00:33:53,610
♪ May the scenery stay simple
and carry you past regret ♪

774
00:33:54,180 --> 00:33:57,160
♪ Love deeply whatever comes to meet you ♪

775
00:33:57,690 --> 00:34:00,760
♪ And let those who leave be buried
under snow on the hills ♪

776
00:34:01,410 --> 00:34:03,950
♪ May you come home covered in dust ♪

777
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:08,040
♪ Held by what you love
as you roam the world and return ♪

778
00:34:09,179 --> 00:34:13,510
♪ Saying she was so beautiful
in front of the door ♪

779
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:13,710
Alright.

780
00:34:14,550 --> 00:34:15,360
We're here.

781
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:17,760
This whole building is ours.

782
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:25,760
The tumor has large draining veins

783
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:27,000
both in front of and behind it.

784
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:29,150
The one behind it
should be the central sulcal vein.

785
00:34:29,150 --> 00:34:30,280
We have to protect it.

786
00:34:30,280 --> 00:34:31,280
Set the bipolar forceps to 15.

787
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:32,000
Okay.

788
00:34:32,190 --> 00:34:33,030
Get the microsurgical dissector

789
00:34:33,030 --> 00:34:34,000
and scissors ready.

790
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:34,670
Okay.

791
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,960
I'll first free the draining vein

792
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:39,000
and then sever the tumor's attachment

793
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,130
to the falx cerebri.

794
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:42,070
After decompressing the area by removing

795
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:44,190
the tumor in sections,
I'll expose the motor cortex.

796
00:34:44,190 --> 00:34:45,590
That's a good plan.

797
00:34:46,960 --> 00:34:49,400
But freeing the vein is delicate work.

798
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:50,800
Be careful.

799
00:34:51,110 --> 00:34:51,960
Don't worry.

800
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,060
Micro-dissector.

801
00:34:57,030 --> 00:34:57,840
Liu,

802
00:34:58,070 --> 00:34:58,880
has

803
00:34:59,030 --> 00:35:01,160
President Long contacted you lately?

804
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:02,150
No.

805
00:35:03,960 --> 00:35:05,070
It's very strange.

806
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:06,110
Well, he's usually

807
00:35:06,110 --> 00:35:07,550
such a show-off,

808
00:35:07,920 --> 00:35:09,280
but now we can't even reach him.

809
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:10,410
No one can reach him.

810
00:35:11,150 --> 00:35:13,920
Is he really going to retire completely?

811
00:35:14,150 --> 00:35:14,960
Let him retire.

812
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,290
Isn't that a good thing?

813
00:35:16,510 --> 00:35:17,440
That won't do.

814
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:20,960
If President Long retires for good,

815
00:35:21,150 --> 00:35:22,280
won't Huang go from acting president

816
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,800
to permanent president?

817
00:35:24,150 --> 00:35:25,080
What a headache.

818
00:35:25,400 --> 00:35:26,400
Micro-scissors.

819
00:35:27,630 --> 00:35:28,440
What?

820
00:35:28,630 --> 00:35:30,480
You have some kind of beef with Huang?

821
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:31,280
No.

822
00:35:31,480 --> 00:35:32,710
Don't talk nonsense.

823
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,230
What I mean is,

824
00:35:35,230 --> 00:35:37,480
we were all colleagues.

825
00:35:38,030 --> 00:35:40,440
Huang's professional title
isn't even as high as mine,

826
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:42,590
and suddenly he's become the president.

827
00:35:42,590 --> 00:35:44,960
And he's
throwing his weight around more every day.

828
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:46,400
He really loves putting on airs.

829
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:47,670
I actually think

830
00:35:48,070 --> 00:35:50,110
Huang is well suited to be the president.

831
00:35:50,110 --> 00:35:50,880
Why?

832
00:35:51,880 --> 00:35:53,080
Haven't you noticed?

833
00:35:53,630 --> 00:35:56,230
He's getting more and more
like Long Dongdong.

834
00:35:59,400 --> 00:36:00,400
President Huang.

835
00:36:04,070 --> 00:36:04,880
Hello, President Huang.

836
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:05,550
Hello.

837
00:36:11,590 --> 00:36:12,400
President.

838
00:36:13,230 --> 00:36:13,960
Long.

839
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:15,280
Where have you been?

840
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:16,520
Keep your voice down.

841
00:36:16,840 --> 00:36:18,280
I missed you so much.

842
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:19,760
Well...

843
00:36:19,840 --> 00:36:21,670
Since you became the new president,

844
00:36:21,670 --> 00:36:23,270
you've been quite busy, huh?

845
00:36:23,360 --> 00:36:25,620
It's been a while
since we had a drink, eh?

846
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:27,660
President, you're finally back.

847
00:36:28,030 --> 00:36:29,230
You have no idea how much has been

848
00:36:29,230 --> 00:36:30,440
-going on at the hospital lately...
-Don't tell me!

849
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:32,030
I don't want to hear it.

850
00:36:33,320 --> 00:36:34,190
Alright then.

851
00:36:34,190 --> 00:36:35,320
I'll report to you tomorrow.

852
00:36:35,320 --> 00:36:36,360
Whenever you report to me,

853
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:37,220
I won't listen.

854
00:36:38,150 --> 00:36:40,480
Besides, what would you even report to me?

855
00:36:40,630 --> 00:36:41,630
Well, so you came back...

856
00:36:41,630 --> 00:36:42,550
came back specifically,

857
00:36:42,550 --> 00:36:43,920
j-just to drink with me?

858
00:36:43,920 --> 00:36:44,850
Come on, cheers.

859
00:36:53,590 --> 00:36:54,230
Lately,

860
00:36:54,230 --> 00:36:56,560
I've been watching the weather forecast.

861
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:59,920
Looks like heavy snow is coming.

862
00:37:04,030 --> 00:37:05,400
Now I finally get it.

863
00:37:05,400 --> 00:37:07,800
You're worried about Liu Zhengliang, huh?

864
00:37:08,030 --> 00:37:09,230
C-Can I ask you something?

865
00:37:09,230 --> 00:37:11,030
Why do you care about him so much?

866
00:37:11,590 --> 00:37:12,990
Don't you care about him?

867
00:37:14,110 --> 00:37:14,800
I've heard

868
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:16,360
that since you became the president,

869
00:37:16,360 --> 00:37:17,820
you've been having people

870
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:19,070
bring all kinds of daily necessities

871
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:20,190
to the storage room

872
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:22,190
he's staying in.

873
00:37:23,150 --> 00:37:24,320
Isn't his apartment gone now?

874
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:25,780
Since it's gone, I just...

875
00:37:26,070 --> 00:37:27,800
He hasn't found a new place yet,

876
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:29,590
so I got him some things.

877
00:37:29,590 --> 00:37:31,190
I'll help him in any way I can.

878
00:37:31,230 --> 00:37:32,710
This kid Liu Zhengliang…

879
00:37:34,190 --> 00:37:34,710
You...

880
00:37:34,800 --> 00:37:35,840
This person, j-just...

881
00:37:35,840 --> 00:37:36,630
He's...

882
00:37:37,230 --> 00:37:39,110
When you first meet him
and get to know him,

883
00:37:39,110 --> 00:37:40,710
his personality and temper

884
00:37:40,710 --> 00:37:41,670
can seem pretty difficult,

885
00:37:41,670 --> 00:37:42,440
you know?

886
00:37:42,510 --> 00:37:44,370
But once you've known him a while,

887
00:37:44,590 --> 00:37:45,510
you'll find

888
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:47,930
he's really kind-hearted.

889
00:37:49,030 --> 00:37:50,760
I knew I wasn't wrong about you.

890
00:38:02,670 --> 00:38:05,110
Look, the doctors
at our Xiaoximen Hospital

891
00:38:05,110 --> 00:38:06,240
might not be the best

892
00:38:06,440 --> 00:38:08,240
when it comes to medical skills.

893
00:38:09,190 --> 00:38:10,190
But I think

894
00:38:11,550 --> 00:38:13,070
even the finest medical skills

895
00:38:13,070 --> 00:38:14,550
can't replace the human touch.

896
00:38:14,550 --> 00:38:15,230
Right.

897
00:38:16,030 --> 00:38:17,400
It's not only hospitals
with the best doctors

898
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:19,530
that deserve to keep their doors open.

899
00:38:19,840 --> 00:38:20,630
Long.

900
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:22,230
Here's to you.

901
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:23,230
Don't toast me.

902
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:24,970
Toast Xiaoximen Hospital.

903
00:38:26,110 --> 00:38:27,440
To Xiaoximen Hospital.

904
00:38:43,670 --> 00:38:44,670
Are you nervous?

905
00:38:46,670 --> 00:38:47,760
I'm not nervous.

906
00:38:48,440 --> 00:38:49,240
Just awkward.

907
00:38:52,110 --> 00:38:53,370
You asked them to come?

908
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:55,920
They knew it was going to snow,

909
00:38:55,920 --> 00:38:57,320
so they came on their own.

910
00:38:58,510 --> 00:38:59,510
Really!

911
00:39:01,510 --> 00:39:02,760
Why do I keep losing?

912
00:39:02,760 --> 00:39:04,020
Because you're a noob.

913
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:05,880
Practice more if you're a noob.

914
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:06,320
Exactly.

915
00:39:06,320 --> 00:39:07,880
When have you ever won?

916
00:39:08,030 --> 00:39:09,230
What do you mean?

917
00:39:09,230 --> 00:39:10,000
You don't want us here

918
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:11,000
because we're getting in the way

919
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:11,920
of you two dating, huh?

920
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:12,800
Not that.

921
00:39:13,670 --> 00:39:14,840
Don't you guys have things of your own

922
00:39:14,840 --> 00:39:15,590
to do?

923
00:39:15,840 --> 00:39:17,840
It's not like we can't spare one day.

924
00:39:18,630 --> 00:39:19,440
We only get

925
00:39:19,510 --> 00:39:21,310
about 30,000 days in a lifetime.

926
00:39:21,590 --> 00:39:23,650
We should enjoy them however we want.

927
00:39:23,710 --> 00:39:24,960
Look, I even brought my guitar today

928
00:39:24,960 --> 00:39:26,400
to liven things up.

929
00:39:26,510 --> 00:39:27,670
I finished delivering goods for my sis

930
00:39:27,670 --> 00:39:29,130
and had nowhere else to go,

931
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:30,920
so I came to hang out with you.

932
00:39:31,280 --> 00:39:33,360
Everyone saw the weather forecast,

933
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:34,440
knew it was going to snow today,

934
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,500
and came to see you.

935
00:39:36,230 --> 00:39:37,230
But not me.

936
00:39:37,230 --> 00:39:38,400
I sold my apartment,

937
00:39:38,400 --> 00:39:39,530
so now I'm homeless.

938
00:39:40,070 --> 00:39:41,470
Well, thank you for that.

939
00:39:41,760 --> 00:39:44,000
If the snow really starts falling

940
00:39:44,320 --> 00:39:45,360
and you're fine,

941
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:45,840
can we

942
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:46,920
go back then?

943
00:39:47,030 --> 00:39:48,230
What if I'm not fine then?

944
00:39:48,230 --> 00:39:48,760
If you are not,

945
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:50,190
we'll carry you straight to the hospital.

946
00:39:50,190 --> 00:39:51,230
Aren't we already at the hospital?

947
00:39:51,230 --> 00:39:52,880
Why are you such a killjoy?

948
00:39:53,110 --> 00:39:54,000
We came all this way to see you,

949
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:54,880
and now you're trying to drive us away?

950
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:56,550
I didn't drive anyone away, did I?

951
00:39:56,550 --> 00:39:57,440
Hurry up and play your cards.

952
00:39:57,440 --> 00:39:58,320
This round, I'm going to

953
00:39:58,320 --> 00:39:59,800
win back everything I've lost.

954
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:01,200
You go. You lost just now.

955
00:40:02,030 --> 00:40:02,760
Play your cards.

956
00:40:02,760 --> 00:40:03,590
I'll go. I'll go.

957
00:40:03,590 --> 00:40:04,320
Let him play.

958
00:40:04,400 --> 00:40:05,800
You don't even know who goes first,

959
00:40:05,800 --> 00:40:06,280
and you're still playing...

960
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:07,150
Stop talking. Hurry.

961
00:40:07,150 --> 00:40:08,630
That's how the pros play.

962
00:40:08,630 --> 00:40:09,360
One.

963
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,230
I had several jokers last round,

964
00:40:10,230 --> 00:40:11,480
but this round, none.

965
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:12,110
Six.

966
00:40:13,710 --> 00:40:14,510
Joker.

967
00:40:14,550 --> 00:40:16,070
-What are you doing?
-What are you doing?

968
00:40:16,070 --> 00:40:16,480
Joker.

969
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:17,630
What are you doing?

970
00:40:17,270 --> 00:40:20,640
♪ The melting snow and the warm wind ♪

971
00:40:17,630 --> 00:40:18,320
You have a killer hand or something?

972
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:19,280
What the heck is your hand?

973
00:40:19,280 --> 00:40:20,070
What do you mean?

974
00:40:20,070 --> 00:40:20,920
Why do you have so many cards?

975
00:40:20,830 --> 00:40:23,130
♪ The flowers bloom again ♪

976
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:22,230
Why do you have so many cards?

977
00:40:22,230 --> 00:40:23,760
Wait for me to sort my cards!

978
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:26,100
♪ You and I ♪

979
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:30,670
♪ Travel light ♪

980
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:38,060
♪ Put the past weighing on my back
into the moon ♪

981
00:40:39,470 --> 00:40:44,630
♪ Longing makes me wake up ♪

982
00:40:45,430 --> 00:40:49,350
♪ To the open window♪

983
00:40:50,110 --> 00:40:56,740
♪ Softly, the person in my dream
is like the moonlight ♪

984
00:40:57,340 --> 00:41:01,480
♪ Falling on my heart softly
and taking me ♪

985
00:40:57,590 --> 00:41:01,290
[Smart Healthcare, Building the Future Together;
Safeguarding Your Health]

986
00:41:01,720 --> 00:41:04,280
♪ To our old familiar place ♪

987
00:41:04,980 --> 00:41:11,370
♪ Slowly, the petals falls to the center
of the lake when I miss you ♪

988
00:41:12,250 --> 00:41:16,320
♪ Ripples echo through the years,
with our shadows faced each other ♪

989
00:41:12,280 --> 00:41:13,540
It's not going to snow.

990
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:14,840
You should head back.

991
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:15,510
Exactly.

992
00:41:15,510 --> 00:41:16,480
Go back and rest.

993
00:41:16,700 --> 00:41:22,050
♪ We were together on the way we came ♪

994
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:18,070
I'm off to the internet café, sis!

995
00:41:18,070 --> 00:41:19,280
Call me if you need anything!

996
00:41:19,280 --> 00:41:21,080
Don't stay out playing too late!

997
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:32,540
Where are you going? I'll give you a ride.

998
00:41:32,550 --> 00:41:34,280
No need. I'll just get a cab.

999
00:41:40,190 --> 00:41:41,590
You sang really well.

1000
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:01,000
I'll leave it here for you, okay?

1001
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:02,360
Okay, leave it there.

1002
00:42:11,840 --> 00:42:12,670
Thank you.

1003
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:17,760
Thank you for being willing to like me,

1004
00:42:19,190 --> 00:42:20,880
someone who is cold, dull,

1005
00:42:21,110 --> 00:42:22,360
boring, fragile,

1006
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:24,420
arrogant, and conceited—

1007
00:42:25,440 --> 00:42:27,550
and who still needs to hibernate.

1008
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:37,970
I've wanted to say this for a long time.

1009
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,230
Ai Chen.

1010
00:42:46,190 --> 00:42:47,110
I like you.
